line	<str>I told Servius and Attala what I'd discovered. Servius left to inform Queen Zyanyi while Attala set out to find and deal with Teumo.</str>
line	<str>I entered Neypotzli and encountered Eyatlalli. She gave me a Keystone Fragment which I used to find the Old One Keystone that Ennius and Furia were looking for. However, I wasn't able to stop them before they could take it. Although they got away, they left behind a pair of Emissaries. However, I was able to defeat them.</str>
line	<str>I spoke with Attala about what happened with the Old One Keystone and she told me that Teumo was able to escape from Cam Torum, resulting in the Twilight Emissaries having everything they needed to access the Crypt of Tonali.</str>
line	<str> I travelled to the Crypt of Tonali in the Tlati Rainforest and met up with Queen Zyanyi and Captain Vibia. We tried our best to fight off the Twilight Emissaries attacking the Crypt, but thanks to Teumo, they were able to make it through to the inner section. However, we did at least manage to rescue Itzla after they did so.</str>
line	<str> Queen zyanyi, Captain Vibia and I followed the Emissaries deeper into the Crypt. We soon encountered Ennius and Furia, who had been abandoned by Metzli. Furia revealed that unlike Ennius, she'd never actually believed the two were Ralos and Ranul reborn. Instead, she believed Metzli would help her overthrow Queen Zyanyi.</str>
line	<str>Queen Zyanyi offered Ennius and Furia the chance to surrender, but Ennius refused. As a result, we had no choice but to fight and kill him. However, Furia was able to escape and follow Metzli down into the Caverns beneath the Crypt. Despite having only just been rescued, Itzla volunteered to join me in following the two down into the Caverns.</str>
line	<str>Itzla and I travelled down into the Caverns beneath the Crypt of Tonali. We explored them, but couldn't find Furia or Metzli. However, we instead found some Old One Ruins.</str>
line	<str>Itzla and I entered the Old One Ruins and found Metzli. She revelaed the Ruins to be Mokhaiotl, an Archive built by the Old Ones before they went extinct. She also revealed that she never believed in the Final Dawn. Instead she was simply using Ennius, Furia and the Twilight Emissaries to find and access Mokhaiotl in the hopes of claiming the knowledge of the Old Ones for herself. Metzli then attacked us, but we were able to fight her off.</str>
line	<col=800000>Despite being injured, <col=800000>Metzli</col> was able to flee deeper into the <col=800000>Ruins</col>. <col=800000>Itzla</col> and I followed her and found her in an <col=800000>Emtpy Chamber</col>. Having completely searched the <col=800000>Ruins</col>, <col=800000>Metzli</col> came to the conclusion they were empty and accepted defeat. However, beforee we could do anything with her, <col=800000>Furia</col> arrived and killed her. <col=800000>Itzla</col> then took <col=800000>Furia</col> back to the surface, but I decided to stay behind and look around some more. I should see if I can find out why the <col=800000>Ruins</col> are empty.</col>
step	22	-	Quest Complete
line	<str>I spoke to Servius, Teokan of Ralos in the Sunrise Palace in Civitas illa Fortis. He took me to meet with Queen Zyanyi Arkan, who tasked me with helping to rescue her son, Prince Itzla Arkan, from the Twilight Emissaries. She told me to go to the Twilight Temple to gather information on the Emissaries' plans for Itzla.</str>
line	<str>I travelled to the Twilight Temple and witnessed Metzli giving a speech to her followers with Ennius and Furia at her side. During the speech, Itzla was brought out from a Dungeon directly below the Temple.</str>
line	<str>I entered the Dungeon below the Twilight Temple and snuck into Metzli's Chamber. There, I overheard her revealing to Furia that she'd moved Itzla elsewhere.</str>
line	<str>I explored Metzli's Chamber and found a Message that might be of use. A Guard found me and took the Message from me, but I was able to defeat him and get it back. The Message revealed the location of a Cultist Safe House in Civitas illa Fortis.</str>
line	<str> I returned to Queen Zyanyi in Civitas illa Fortis and told her what I'd discovered. She directed me to meet with Captain Vibia at the Cultist Safe House. The two of us must then gain entry into the House and capture Forebearer Janus, the cultist living there.</str>
line	<str>I met with Captain Vibia at the Cultist Safe House in south western Civitas illa Fortis. While she kept watch, I found a Window for us to use to get into the House, distracted a Dog on the other side, and then unlocked a Door leading to the rest of the House</str>
line	<str>After gaining access to the House, we started preparing for Forebearer Janus to return. To do so, I created a Makeshift Blackjack and gave Captain Vibia a Sack. Once he arrived, Captain Vibia used the Sack to restrain him and I knocked him out with the Blackjack. Captain Vibia then departed to fetch Queen Zyanyi.</str>
line	<str>Queen Zyanyi arrived at the House and asked to be left alone with Forebearer Janus so that she could interrogate him. By the time we returned later, Janus was dead. However, before he died, he told Queen Zyanyi of the Emissaries' plan to use Itzla to gain entry into the Crypt of Tonali in the Tlati Rainforest. He claimed this was due to the Crypt containing a path to Mokhaiotl. Janus also revealed that the Emissaries were seeking help from some Dwarves in Cam Torum to achieve entry into the crypt.</str>
line	<str>I journeyed to Cam Torum with Queen Zyanyi and Servius. There, we met with Highlord Katlo. He claimed he wasn't aware of any Emissaries in Cam Torum, but his advisor, Attala, convinced him to let us investigate anyway. Queen Zyanyi departed for the Tlati Rainforest, leaving Servius and I to find the Emissaries with Attala's help.</str>
line	<str>Servius and I met with Attala in the Cam Torum Market. I searched the house and found a Secret Tunnel. I explored the Tunnel and was able to spy on a meeting between Teumo, Ennius and Furia. During the meeting, Teumo agreed to help them gain access to the Crypt of the Tonali, but first asked them to retrieve an Old One Keystone from within Neypotzli for him.</str>
line	<str>I told Servius and Attala what I'd discovered. Servius left to inform Queen Zyanyi while Attala set out to find and deal with Teumo.</str>
line	<str>I entered Neypotzli and encountered Eyatlalli. She gave me a Keystone Fragment which I used to find the Old One Keystone that Ennius and Furia were looking for. However, I wasn't able to stop them before they could take it. Although they got away, they left behind a pair of Emissaries. However, I was able to defeat them.</str>
line	<str>I spoke with Attala about what happened with the Old One Keystone and she told me that Teumo was able to escape from Cam Torum, resulting in the Twilight Emissaries having everything they needed to access the Crypt of Tonali.</str>
line	<str> I travelled to the Crypt of Tonali in the Tlati Rainforest and met up with Queen Zyanyi and Captain Vibia. We tried our best to fight off the Twilight Emissaries attacking the Crypt, but thanks to Teumo, they were able to make it through to the inner section. However, we did at least manage to rescue Itzla after they did so.</str>
line	<str> Queen zyanyi, Captain Vibia and I followed the Emissaries deeper into the Crypt. We soon encountered Ennius and Furia, who had been abandoned by Metzli. Furia revealed that unlike Ennius, she'd never actually believed the two were Ralos and Ranul reborn. Instead, she believed Metzli would help her overthrow Queen Zyanyi.</str>
line	<str>Queen Zyanyi offered Ennius and Furia the chance to surrender, but Ennius refused. As a result, we had no choice but to fight and kill him. However, Furia was able to escape and follow Metzli down into the Caverns beneath the Crypt. Despite having only just been rescued, Itzla volunteered to join me in following the two down into the Caverns.</str>
line	<str>Itzla and I travelled down into the Caverns beneath the Crypt of Tonali. We explored them, but couldn't find Furia or Metzli. However, we instead found some Old One Ruins.</str>
line	<str>Itzla and I entered the Old One Ruins and found Metzli. She revelaed the Ruins to be Mokhaiotl, an Archive built by the Old Ones before they went extinct. She also revealed that she never believed in the Final Dawn. Instead she was simply using Ennius, Furia and the Twilight Emissaries to find and access Mokhaiotl in the hopes of claiming the knowledge of the Old Ones for herself. Metzli then attacked us, but we were able to fight her off.</str>
line	<str>Despite being injured, Metzli was able to flee deeper into the Ruins. Itzla and I followed her and found her in an Empty Chamber. Having completely searched the Ruins, Metzli came to the conclusion they were empty and accepted defeat. However, before we could do anything with her, Furia arrived and killed her Itzla then took Furia back to the surface, but I decided to stay behind and look around some more.</str>
line	<str>I looked around the Empty Chamber where Itzla and I found Metzli. I found information that revealed the Ruins were indeed meant to be an Archive for the Old Ones, but that work was never completed due to the presence of some sort of Creature deep beneath the Archive. I also found two statues with the names Ralos and Ranul on them.</str>
line	<str>I returned to the Crypt of Tonali and met with Itzla and Queen Zyanyi. Itzla suggested that Furia be allowed to live so as not to make another martyr for the surviving Twilight Emissaries. The Queen agreed. She then thanked us for stopping Metzli before returning to Civitas illa Fortis. Itzla then thanked me himself and presented me with his sword, the Arkan Blade, before departing for Civitas illa Fortis himself.</str>
line	<col=ff0000>QUEST COMPLETE!</col>
